from pathlib import Path
import json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];A=ROOT/'art';raw=A/'raw'
ledger=json.loads((A/'ledger.json').read_text())
lines=['# Thief of Dawn art report','','PixelLab requests used only `tools/pixellab.py` (`call`, `poll`, `get`, `spent`); no direct API client. No engine, data, tests, or README changes. No commits.','','## Cost and provenance','','Total measured spend: **$'+f"{json.loads((A/'spend.json').read_text())['spent_usd']:.5f}"+'**. The $1 wrapper hard cap was used throughout. Initial requests and planned retries used a $0.90 planning ceiling; a late shade-hurt repair used the explicitly reserved $0.10 fix allowance. A delayed charge for the DNS-interrupted Morrow job arrived during that repair; both are included in the real total.','','The wrapper can record zero for a synchronous image when its balance charge arrives just after its final balance read. The real final spend includes these delayed charges. Ledger cost below is the wrapper measurement, with response usage separately shown for reconciliation; response usage is not substituted for real total spend.','','| Item | Endpoint | Ledger cost USD | Response usage | Prompt |','|---|---|---:|---:|---|']
for c in ledger['calls']:
 name=c['note'];p=raw/(name+'.request.json');r=raw/(name+'.json')
 payload=json.loads(p.read_text())['payload'] if p.exists() else {}
 prompt=' / '.join(str(payload[k]) for k in ['description','action','lower_description','transition_description'] if k in payload).replace('|','/')
 result=json.loads(r.read_text()) if r.exists() else {};usage=result.get('usage') or {};u=(f"${usage['usd']:.5f}" if 'usd' in usage else json.dumps(usage))
 lines.append(f"| {name} | {c['endpoint']} | {c['cost_usd']:.5f} | {u} | {prompt} |")
lines+=['','## Processing and approximations','','- Frames: 64×64 RGBA, binary alpha, right-facing references, feet anchor (32,60), scale derived from each actor’s base reference with a documented correction for undersized legacy ledge poses; nearest-neighbour only. The v3 reference frame is omitted from the run loop.','- Every animation derives from that actor’s one reference image; Kael is unarmed in locomotion and uses the sword in combat clips.',('- Vesh uses a dedicated PixelLab grey-steel, green-skinned, red-cloaked reference and reference-conditioned animations.' if (raw/'vesh.json').exists() else '- Vesh is a Pillow steel/green/red colour variant of shade; no new armour rig.'),('- Morrow uses a dedicated PixelLab tattered violet scholar reference with pale mask and Lantern, plus reference-conditioned animations. Attack is a Lantern spell, not a sword slash.' if (raw/'morrow.json').exists() else '- Morrow is a taller Pillow shade variant with pale mask and robe overlay; attached Lantern and separate cast are absent.'),'- Props are generated at twice the required dimensions to satisfy the API minimum canvas area, then reduced with nearest-neighbour scaling.','- Torch has three local flame variants derived from one PixelLab prop, rather than three separately generated frames.','- Backgrounds generated at 240×128 and doubled to 480×256; title at 240×136 doubled and vertically cropped to 480×270 with local lettering.','- Tiles are cut from PixelLab sidescroller sheets; bg is a darkened solid tile, pillar and window are local compositions of generated masonry.','- No optional Sarai portrait, Kael idle_sword/crouch/land, or Morrow cast. The engine can use its documented placeholders for absent optional assets.','','## Contract and rebuild','','All generated art outputs are under `assets/` and `art/`. The explicitly requested source entry point is `tools/art_build.py`; its implementation and build recipes live in `art/`. Rebuild offline with `python -B tools/art_build.py`. Pillow 13.0.0 and its license metadata are archived under git-ignored `art/raw/python_deps/` for this Python 3.12/Linux environment; the build automatically uses that local copy if Pillow is not installed. No network is required.','','Raw responses and requests are retained in git-ignored `art/raw/`. API keys were never copied into them. `art/contact_sheet.png` includes every output image, grouped into labelled character strips and rendered ×2. Complete source Wang atlases and rejected attempts appear after the delivered assets.']
if (A/'cost_summary.json').exists():
 lines+=['','## Balance reconciliation','','```json',(A/'cost_summary.json').read_text(),'```']
review=json.loads((A/'review_state.json').read_text())
lines+=['','## Review selections','','Generated clips can change proportions or camera direction. Rejected attempts remain under art/raw and appear as labelled rejected strips on the contact sheet.']
lines+=['- '+note for note in review.get('notes',[])]
lines+=['- Rejected '+k+': '+v for k,v in review.get('rejected',{}).items()]
if (A/'failures.json').exists():
 lines+=['','## API failures','', '```json',(A/'failures.json').read_text(),'```']
validation=json.loads((A/'validation.json').read_text())
lines+=['','## Contract validation','','```json',json.dumps(validation,indent=2),'```']
if (A/'rebuild_check.json').exists():
 lines+=['','## Offline rebuild verification','','```json',(A/'rebuild_check.json').read_text(),'```']
(A/'ART_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
